Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:32:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(methane): deepen the wetland anoxia scalar below the
 water table (C-18)

Ledger C-18 (paper V2), parameter wetland_anoxia_catotelm, negative (off)
by default. The wetland anoxia scalar was mino2lim (0.2) in every thawed
layer. That matches peatland litter bags near the surface with CENTURY's
litter rates, but leaves saturated deep peat turning over 3-10 times faster
than catotelm estimates (1e-4 to 3e-5 per year; Clymo 1984, Kleinen et al.
2012). With the parameter set, the scalar falls with depth d below the water
table as floor + (mino2lim - floor) exp(-d/wetland_anoxia_efold), the HPM
form (Frolking et al. 2010, eq. 9, c2 = 0.3 m). The inundated share has its
table at the surface and the rest at the host water table; above the table
the scalar stays mino2lim.

---
 Makefile | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

